            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 22-year-old male patient, admitted on 07/12/2020 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection (PCR-positive nasopharyngeal swab). On admission, he presented with fever, dry cough, and dyspnoea. Chest X-ray and CT thorax demonstrated bilateral ground-glass opacities consistent with COVID-19 pneumonia. Blood tests revealed elevated CRP and mild lymphopenia. Oxygen saturation was reduced, requiring supplemental oxygen therapy. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed mild hypoxaemic respiratory failure. The patient was treated with dexamethasone and anticoagulation. Vital signs and pulse oximetry were monitored continuously. Physiotherapy was initiated early to support respiratory recovery. Clinical condition improved steadily, and the patient was discharged on 20/12/2020 in a recovering state. Please ensure outpatient follow-up within two weeks including repeat pulmonary assessment. Do not hesitate to contact me with any queries.</div>"
            },
